                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "The COPYCÆT corpus was created as part of the NWO-funded project Old English Renewed: Tracing Transitional English in the Twelfth Century (grant number: PGW.21.031) and consists of c. 135,000 words. It features transcriptions of later manuscript copies of ten of Ælfric of Eynsham's (c. 955–c.1010) Catholic Homilies."
